# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# pfmatch
#
# The working tree is ~6.9 GB; the package is ~1.1 MB. Everything large here is
# either a public source file that can be re-downloaded or a derived artifact
# that regenerates from inputs/ plus the BMF. What IS tracked is the code, the
# small public fixtures, and the hand-adjudicated ground truth -- that last one
# cannot be regenerated at any price.
#
# Note the `dir/*` form rather than `dir/`: git cannot re-include a file whose
# parent directory is excluded, so the negations below only work this way.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---- derived artifacts, caches, checkpoints (6.3 GB) ----------------------
data-dev/*
# ... except the audit samples the verdicts in dev/maybe-verdicts.csv key to
!data-dev/AUDIT-MAYBE-100.csv
!data-dev/AUDIT-NO-100.csv
!data-dev/AUDIT-NO-100-PROBE.csv
!data-dev/AUDIT-OOS-100.csv

# ... and the ground truth, which the header above already says is tracked and
# which these rules did not in fact cover. Hand adjudication is the one thing
# here that cannot be regenerated from inputs/ plus the BMF at any price, and
# until 2026-10-23 all of it lived only in a Dropbox folder. ~7 MB in total.
!data-dev/PF-TRUTH.csv
!data-dev/PF-TRUTH-V2.csv
!data-dev/LIFT-CROSSWALK-V2.csv

# ... and the address-triangulation set: 2,853 informative cases over 4,326
# address groups, where one organisation is written several ways and the
# renderings got different verdicts. TRIANGULATION-GROUPS is the artifact worth
# trusting -- it carries no labels, only (grant_id, group_id), and feeds
# pf_consistency(). SAMPLE is an adjudication queue at ~50-60% precision, not
# an answer key. See dev/build-triangulation-sample.R for which is which.
# ... and the adjudication round's drawn frame. 400 rows, and in principle
# regenerable -- dev/draw-round-stage1.R plus seed 20261102 -- but only against
# data-dev/TRI-V2-MATCH.rds, which is 651 MB and not tracked. The labels will
# key to these grant_ids, so losing the draw would orphan them, which puts it
# in the same class as the audit samples above.
!data-dev/ADJ-ROUND-STAGE1.csv
# ... and the dealt shards. The case files and the EMPTY templates regenerate
# from the draw plus dev/deal-round-stage1.R and seed 20261103; a FILLED
# template is hand adjudication, which the header above says is the one thing
# here that cannot be regenerated at any price, and it arrives by being written
# into these same files. So they are tracked from the moment they are dealt
# rather than from the moment someone remembers to add them. SHARD-KEY names
# the blinded overlap and pf_read_truth() needs it to validate what comes back;
# keeping it out of round-stage1/ is about what a labeler is handed, not about
# what is in git.
!data-dev/round-stage1
!data-dev/round-stage1-key
# ... and two files of the superseded k=8 deal, which is otherwise worthless --
# its templates were empty and the cases regenerate. The key is the only record
# of the overlap imbalance that pf_truth_shards() now deals around (7 and 15
# cases on two labelers against an expectation of 10), and that figure is cited
# in R/shards.R, its roxygen and ADJUDICATION-PREREQS.md 6b.6. The deal is NOT
# reproducible from its seed any more -- the overlap is dealt rather than
# sampled now -- so without this file those three citations point at nothing,
# which is the defect dev/FIGURE-PROVENANCE.md exists to catch.
# Re-include the directory first, then re-exclude its contents: the header
# above says git cannot re-include a file whose parent is excluded.
!data-dev/round-stage1-k8-superseded
data-dev/round-stage1-k8-superseded/*
!data-dev/round-stage1-k8-superseded/SHARD-KEY.csv
!data-dev/round-stage1-k8-superseded/README.md

# ... and the labels that come BACK from a labeler. The dealt templates above
# are tracked because a filled one is adjudication that cannot be regenerated
# at any price; these are those templates filled in. They are model-produced
# rather than hand-produced, so "any price" is really ~$15 and ~700 web
# searches per shard -- but they are still the round's truth, every figure the
# round reports is measured against them, and a web search is not reproducible
# in the way a seed is: re-running the labeler next month queries a different
# web. Same re-include-the-directory-first dance as above. The -limitN files
# are smoke-test output over the first few cases and are deliberately left out.
!data-dev/round-stage1-labelled
data-dev/round-stage1-labelled/*
!data-dev/round-stage1-labelled/*.csv
data-dev/round-stage1-labelled/*-limit[0-9]*.csv

!data-dev/TRIANGULATION-GROUPS.csv
!data-dev/TRIANGULATION-SAMPLE.csv
!data-dev/TRIANGULATION-CANDIDATES.csv
!data-dev/TRIANGULATION-GATED.csv
!data-dev/PF-TRUTH-TRIANGULATED.csv

# ---- source data (625 MB) --------------------------------------------------
inputs/*
# ... except the benchmark fixtures and the NTEE source, all small and public,
# so that a clean clone can run the 1k benchmark and rebuild data/nteev2.rda
!inputs/1k_grants_0*.csv
# ... and the e-file rebuild's equivalents. Kept alongside rather than
# replacing the line above: BASELINE-2026-08 is defined as the benchmark over
# 1k_grants_0*, so overwriting those would make the frozen reference point
# unreproducible.
!inputs/ef1k_grants_0*.csv
# ... and the v2 lift, which BASELINE-2026-10B is defined over, plus the
# independent draw that shows the lift still represents the deduplicated
# population. Same reasoning again: a frozen baseline whose population is not
# in the repository is not reproducible.
!inputs/efv2_1k_grants_0*.csv
!inputs/effresh_1k_grants_0*.csv
!inputs/nteev2-descriptions.csv
!inputs/nteev2-descriptions-tidy-format.csv
!inputs/GTDC*.xlsx

# The BMF (1.7 GB) lives in ../npmatch/data-raw and is never tracked here.
# The 990 Part III extracts (525 MB) are re-downloadable from the GT 990 lake;
# see dev/build-990-text-wide.R for the filenames.

# ---- R build / session -----------------------------------------------------
.Rproj.user/
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata
*.Rproj
*.tar.gz
*.Rcheck/
/data/*.rda.bak

# ---- OS --------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini


# docs/ IS committed: GitHub Pages serves the site from main:/docs.
# Rebuild with pkgdown::build_site() and commit the result.

# The hand-labelled slice (dev/draw-hand-slice.R). Re-include the directory
# first: git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded.
!data-dev/round-stage1-handslice
data-dev/round-stage1-handslice/*
!data-dev/round-stage1-handslice/*.csv
!data-dev/round-stage1-handslice/README.md

# The B2-token-concat top-up (dev/draw-b2-topup.R). Same re-include-the-
# directory-first pattern, and the same exclusions as stage 1: the .rds beside
# each labelled CSV carries the raw API usage/response columns, and a
# -limitN.csv is a smoke test over a few cases rather than the shard.
!data-dev/round-b2-topup
data-dev/round-b2-topup/*
!data-dev/round-b2-topup/*.csv
!data-dev/round-b2-topup-key
data-dev/round-b2-topup-key/*
!data-dev/round-b2-topup-key/*.csv
!data-dev/round-b2-topup-labelled
data-dev/round-b2-topup-labelled/*
!data-dev/round-b2-topup-labelled/*.csv
data-dev/round-b2-topup-labelled/*-limit[0-9]*.csv
